  30:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_interpolate_f32.c **** 
  31:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_interpolate_f32.c **** /**
  32:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_interpolate_f32.c ****  * @defgroup FIR_Interpolate Finite Impulse Response (FIR) Interpolator
  33:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_interpolate_f32.c ****  *
  34:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_interpolate_f32.c ****  * These functions combine an upsampler (zero stuffer) and an FIR filter.
  35:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_interpolate_f32.c ****  * They are used in multirate systems for increasing the sample rate of a signal without introducin
  36:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_interpolate_f32.c ****  * Conceptually, the functions are equivalent to the block diagram below:
  37:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_interpolate_f32.c ****  * \image html FIRInterpolator.gif "Components included in the FIR Interpolator functions"
  38:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_interpolate_f32.c ****  * After upsampling by a factor of <code>L</code>, the signal should be filtered by a lowpass filte
  39:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_interpolate_f32.c ****  * cutoff frequency of <code>1/L</code> in order to eliminate high frequency copies of the spectrum
  40:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_interpolate_f32.c ****  * The user of the function is responsible for providing the filter coefficients.
  41:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_interpolate_f32.c ****  *
  42:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_interpolate_f32.c ****  * The FIR interpolator functions provided in the CMSIS DSP Library combine the upsampler and FIR f
  43:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_interpolate_f32.c ****  * The upsampler inserts <code>L-1</code> zeros between each sample.
  44:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_interpolate_f32.c ****  * Instead of multiplying by these zero values, the FIR filter is designed to skip them.
  45:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_interpolate_f32.c ****  * This leads to an efficient implementation without any wasted effort.
  46:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_interpolate_f32.c ****  * The functions operate on blocks of input and output data.
  47:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_interpolate_f32.c ****  * <code>pSrc</code> points to an array of <code>blockSize</code> input values and
  48:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_interpolate_f32.c ****  * <code>pDst</code> points to an array of <code>blockSize*L</code> output values.
  49:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_interpolate_f32.c ****  *
  50:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_interpolate_f32.c ****  * The library provides separate functions for Q15, Q31, and floating-point data types.
  51:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_interpolate_f32.c ****  *
  52:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_interpolate_f32.c ****  * \par Algorithm:
  53:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_interpolate_f32.c ****  * The functions use a polyphase filter structure:
  54:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_interpolate_f32.c ****  * <pre>
  55:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_interpolate_f32.c ****  *    y[n] = b[0] * x[n] + b[L]   * x[n-1] + ... + b[L*(phaseLength-1)] * x[n-phaseLength+1]
  56:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_interpolate_f32.c ****  *    y[n+1] = b[1] * x[n] + b[L+1] * x[n-1] + ... + b[L*(phaseLength-1)+1] * x[n-phaseLength+1]
  57:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_interpolate_f32.c ****  *    ...
  58:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_interpolate_f32.c ****  *    y[n+(L-1)] = b[L-1] * x[n] + b[2*L-1] * x[n-1] + ....+ b[L*(phaseLength-1)+(L-1)] * x[n-phase
  59:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_interpolate_f32.c ****  * </pre>
  60:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_interpolate_f32.c ****  * This approach is more efficient than straightforward upsample-then-filter algorithms.
  61:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_interpolate_f32.c ****  * With this method the computation is reduced by a factor of <code>1/L</code> when compared to usi
  62:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_interpolate_f32.c ****  * \par
  63:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_interpolate_f32.c ****  * <code>pCoeffs</code> points to a coefficient array of size <code>numTaps</code>.
  64:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_interpolate_f32.c ****  * <code>numTaps</code> must be a multiple of the interpolation factor <code>L</code> and this is c
  65:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_interpolate_f32.c ****  * initialization functions.
  66:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_interpolate_f32.c ****  * Internally, the function divides the FIR filter's impulse response into shorter filters of lengt
  67:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_interpolate_f32.c ****  * <code>phaseLength=numTaps/L</code>.
  68:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_interpolate_f32.c ****  * Coefficients are stored in time reversed order.
  69:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_interpolate_f32.c ****  * \par
  70:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_interpolate_f32.c ****  * <pre>
  71:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_interpolate_f32.c ****  *    {b[numTaps-1], b[numTaps-2], b[N-2], ..., b[1], b[0]}
  72:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_interpolate_f32.c ****  * </pre>
  73:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_interpolate_f32.c ****  * \par
  74:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_interpolate_f32.c ****  * <code>pState</code> points to a state array of size <code>blockSize + phaseLength - 1</code>.
  75:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_interpolate_f32.c ****  * Samples in the state buffer are stored in the order:
  76:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_interpolate_f32.c ****  * \par
  77:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_interpolate_f32.c ****  * <pre>
  78:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_interpolate_f32.c ****  *    {x[n-phaseLength+1], x[n-phaseLength], x[n-phaseLength-1], x[n-phaseLength-2]....x[0], x[1], 
  79:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_interpolate_f32.c ****  * </pre>
  80:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_interpolate_f32.c ****  * The state variables are updated after each block of data is processed, the coefficients are unto
  81:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_interpolate_f32.c ****  *
  82:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_interpolate_f32.c ****  * \par Instance Structure
  83:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_interpolate_f32.c ****  * The coefficients and state variables for a filter are stored together in an instance data struct
  84:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_interpolate_f32.c ****  * A separate instance structure must be defined for each filter.
  85:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_interpolate_f32.c ****  * Coefficient arrays may be shared among several instances while state variable array should be al
  86:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_interpolate_f32.c ****  * There are separate instance structure declarations for each of the 3 supported data types.
ARM GAS  C:\Users\Lamp\AppData\Local\Temp\cc10nfjt.s 			page 3


  87:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_interpolate_f32.c ****  *
  88:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_interpolate_f32.c ****  * \par Initialization Functions
  89:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_interpolate_f32.c ****  * There is also an associated initialization function for each data type.
  90:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_interpolate_f32.c ****  * The initialization function performs the following operations:
  91:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_interpolate_f32.c ****  * - Sets the values of the internal structure fields.
  92:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_interpolate_f32.c ****  * - Zeros out the values in the state buffer.
  93:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_interpolate_f32.c ****  * - Checks to make sure that the length of the filter is a multiple of the interpolation factor.
  94:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_interpolate_f32.c ****  * To do this manually without calling the init function, assign the follow subfields of the instan
  95:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_interpolate_f32.c ****  * L (interpolation factor), pCoeffs, phaseLength (numTaps / L), pState. Also set all of the values
  96:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_interpolate_f32.c ****  *
  97:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_interpolate_f32.c ****  * \par
  98:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_interpolate_f32.c ****  * Use of the initialization function is optional.
  99:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_interpolate_f32.c ****  * However, if the initialization function is used, then the instance structure cannot be placed in
 100:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_interpolate_f32.c ****  * To place an instance structure into a const data section, the instance structure must be manuall
 101:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_interpolate_f32.c ****  * The code below statically initializes each of the 3 different data type filter instance structur
 102:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_interpolate_f32.c ****  * <pre>
 103:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_interpolate_f32.c ****  * arm_fir_interpolate_instance_f32 S = {L, phaseLength, pCoeffs, pState};
 104:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_interpolate_f32.c ****  * arm_fir_interpolate_instance_q31 S = {L, phaseLength, pCoeffs, pState};
 105:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_interpolate_f32.c ****  * arm_fir_interpolate_instance_q15 S = {L, phaseLength, pCoeffs, pState};
 106:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_interpolate_f32.c ****  * </pre>
 107:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_interpolate_f32.c ****  * where <code>L</code> is the interpolation factor; <code>phaseLength=numTaps/L</code> is the
 108:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_interpolate_f32.c ****  * length of each of the shorter FIR filters used internally,
 109:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_interpolate_f32.c ****  * <code>pCoeffs</code> is the address of the coefficient buffer;
 110:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_interpolate_f32.c ****  * <code>pState</code> is the address of the state buffer.
 111:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_interpolate_f32.c ****  * Be sure to set the values in the state buffer to zeros when doing static initialization.
 112:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_interpolate_f32.c ****  *
 113:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_interpolate_f32.c ****  * \par Fixed-Point Behavior
 114:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_interpolate_f32.c ****  * Care must be taken when using the fixed-point versions of the FIR interpolate filter functions.
 115:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_interpolate_f32.c ****  * In particular, the overflow and saturation behavior of the accumulator used in each function mus
 116:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_interpolate_f32.c ****  * Refer to the function specific documentation below for usage guidelines.
 117:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_interpolate_f32.c ****  */
 118:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_interpolate_f32.c **** 
 119:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_interpolate_f32.c **** /**
 120:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_interpolate_f32.c ****  * @addtogroup FIR_Interpolate
 121:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_interpolate_f32.c ****  * @{
 122:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_interpolate_f32.c ****  */
 123:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_interpolate_f32.c **** 
 124:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_interpolate_f32.c **** /**
 125:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_interpolate_f32.c ****  * @brief Processing function for the floating-point FIR interpolator.
 126:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_interpolate_f32.c ****  * @param[in] *S        points to an instance of the floating-point FIR interpolator structure.
 127:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_interpolate_f32.c ****  * @param[in] *pSrc     points to the block of input data.
 128:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_interpolate_f32.c ****  * @param[out] *pDst    points to the block of output data.
 129:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_interpolate_f32.c ****  * @param[in] blockSize number of input samples to process per call.
 130:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_interpolate_f32.c ****  * @return none.
 131:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_interpolate_f32.c ****  */
 132:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_interpolate_f32.c **** #if defined (ARM_MATH_DSP)
 133:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_interpolate_f32.c **** 
 134:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_interpolate_f32.c ****   /* Run the below code for Cortex-M4 and Cortex-M3 */
 135:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_interpolate_f32.c **** 
 136:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_interpolate_f32.c **** void arm_fir_interpolate_f32(
 137:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_interpolate_f32.c ****   const arm_fir_interpolate_instance_f32 * S,
 138:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_interpolate_f32.c ****   float32_t * pSrc,
 139:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_interpolate_f32.c ****   float32_t * pDst,
 140:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_interpolate_f32.c ****   uint32_t blockSize)
 141:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_interpolate_f32.c **** {
 142:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_interpolate_f32.c ****   float32_t *pState = S->pState;                 /* State pointer */
 143:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_interpolate_f32.c ****   float32_t *pCoeffs = S->pCoeffs;               /* Coefficient pointer */
